  "body": "## What changed\n\n- The Fanuc and Doosan DNM posts end a program upright.\n- If a rotary is off zero after the last section, the program end writes these blocks before M30:\n  - `G49`\n  - `G91 G28 Z0` (or `G53 G00 Z<safe_retract>` with `safeRetract` G53)\n  - `G90` (G28 mode only)\n  - `G00 A0. B0.` (only the rotaries off zero; no X/Y/Z word)\n  - `G91 G28 X0 Y0` (G28 mode only)\n- Doosan writes `M11` before and `M10` after the return when A turns.\n- These are the same blocks as the section return of #3466 (PR #3478).\n- A trailing \"Go home\" ask already lifts Z. Then the end writes only the zero angle block.\n- An upright program ends byte for byte as before.\n- `heldRotaries()` and `rotariesToZero()` are now shared by the section return and the program end. The section return output does not change.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/3540-program-end-rotary-return.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe angle words are modal. `onClose()` wrote only the Z and X/Y reference return. The table or the head stayed at the last tilt after M30. On Doosan, G43.4 was also still active at the reference return.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins (new, in the `upright_after_tilt` suite as the submodule `upright_after_tilt/program_end.rs`; no new test binary):\n\n- `program_end::fanuc_returns_rotaries_before_program_end` (G28 and G53 modes)\n- `program_end::doosan_returns_rotaries_before_program_end` (G28 and G53 modes)\n- `program_end::doosan_unclamps_and_clamps_a_at_program_end`\n- `program_end::upright_program_end_adds_no_rotary_return` (control: the upright end is unchanged)\n\nRed before the fix: yes. On unchanged posts, the three return pins failed with \"the program commands B0 before M30\". The upright control passed.\n\nMutation results (each restored after the run):\n\n- `fanuc.cps` from upstream/main: the Fanuc pin is red.\n- `doosan-dnm.cps` from upstream/main: both Doosan pins are red.\n- No `G49` in the Fanuc end: red (\"G49 cancels TCPM before the retract\").\n- `G28 X0 Y0` without `G91` in the Doosan end: red (\"the X/Y home is incremental\").\n- No M11/M10 around the Doosan return: red (\"M11 before the A return\").\n- After each restore: green.\n\nExpected-change updates (each test lists every angle or move word, and the program end adds the return):\n\n- `crates/app/tests/program_units.rs` `rotary_angle_words_are_degrees_in_an_inch_program`: adds `A0.`, `B0.` (tilthead) and `A0.` (Doosan 4th axis).\n- `crates/post/tests/doosan_dnm_post.rs` `doosan_dnm_index_names_only_a_stated_rotary`: adds `M11`, `G00 A0.`, `M10`.\n\nCommands and results on the final head (54878770e, merged with upstream/main db3bb1f7f):\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 145 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled. This includes `app suites: example_catalog`, `example_catalog_adaptive` and `example_catalog_edge_work`.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`: 8 steps (release build, `do_not_touch`, `do_not_touch_adaptive`, `example_catalog`, `lathe_workholding_kinds`, `mcp`, `probe_no_coolant`, `sinker_burn`), 0 failed. The heavy run and the light run were on the head before the merge of upstream/main. That merge brought only `rotary_verify.rs` and two decision files. `rotary_verify` passes on the merged head.\n- `cargo xtask gate light --base upstream/main`: 6 steps, 0 failed.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\n- `examples/catalog/multiaxis/indexed/indexed.nc`: regenerated with `cargo xtask catalog --case multiaxis/indexed`. Only the end blocks change:\n\n```\n M9\n M5\n+G49\n G91 G28 Z0\n-G28 X0 Y0\n+G90\n+G00 A0. B0.\n+G91 G28 X0 Y0\n M30\n```\n\n- The catalog tool also changed the `version` field of `indexed.camproj`. That change is not related, and it is not in this PR.\n- No other `*.nc` or `*.cl` file changed. The example catalog suites pass.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No program ran on a real Fanuc or Doosan control.\n- The Go-home path at the program end (a trailing `AfterOperation home` on a tilted last section) is not pinned. In that path the end writes only `G00` with the zero angles after the existing home.\n- Other rotary posts are not changed:\n  - Tormach keeps its final tilt by the decision of #1594.\n  - Mach4 also keeps its final pose. It is not in the scope of this issue.\n  - Haas and Sinumerik refuse tilted output.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #3787 (draft, `issue/3690-feed-decimals`) changes `ff()` and `feedWord()` in `fanuc.cps` and `doosan-dnm.cps`. This PR changes `uprightAfterTilt()` and `onClose()`. They touch the same files but different functions. The PR that merges second refreshes, and `indexed.nc` can need a regeneration.\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: The Fanuc and Doosan DNM posts return the rotary axes to zero (after G49 and the Z retract) at the end of a program whose last section is tilted.\n\nFixes #3540\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
